Remaining counterexample: `1e-50` is finite and positive in JSON/Python, so it passes DSparkStsCalibration.__post_init__. It underflows to zero in the runtime float32 tensor. The candidate checks only torch.isfinite and therefore installs zero despite the strictly-positive calibration contract. Applying confidence uses logits / sts_temperatures, so this introduces division by zero and saturates nonzero logits rather than providing a valid finite-temperature calibration.
